==Enemy==
Bore Jr. is a glass cannon, with relatively low health but an extremely damaging attack, and the ability to spam [[Mini-Wave]]s if he isn't killed in time.

At 100% strength magnification, his Mini-Waves deal 4,700 damage each, shredding your cats quickly.

==Strategy==
With absurd DPS and a guaranteed chance to create a Mini-Wave with each attack, Bore Jr. is pretty much an enemy version of [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] with the potential to devastate your entire army if left unchecked. Therefore, it is imperative that you remove him from the field as soon as possible.

Thankfully, Bore Jr. has mediocre health, so burst damage can be an effective response to him, as is stacking a group of attackers beforehand, though later in the game Bore Jr. reaches magnifications of up to 180%, not only skyrocketing his damage output but also making him surprisingly resilient. Here are some recommended units that can help dispose of Bore Jr.:
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With his [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] Awakened Bahamut Cat is an extremely reliable counter to Bore Jr., being able to instantly kill him at all magnifications before he starts causing chaos. Bonus points if you can damage other enemy units nearby.
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]]: Similarly, Idi can also take out Bore Jr. swiftly, though 180% Bore Jrs. will hang on with a sliver of health and Idi's lack of pierce compared to Talented Bahamut makes her slightly harder to use.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]]: At Lv.43 and above, Teacher BearCat can oneshot a 100% Bore Jr. Other than that, his quick foreswing means he could be useful for finishing off a weakened Bore Jr. Though, you'll need good timing and/or a lack of stepping stones for Bore Jr.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train cannot oneshot a Bore Jr. by itself, but its high bulk and unmatched speed helps it be a reliable finisher. The combination of a Lv.50 Jellycat's Wave Attack and a Lv.50 Bullet Train Cat can take out the 150% Bore Jr. in [[Revival of Origin]], and only needs chip damage to neutralize stronger Bore Jrs.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]]: Jellycat's Cat's far-reaching Wave Attack can help chip down Bore Jr. as he approaches the frontline, helping set up a kill for other units.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]]: Hitman Cat can oneshot 150% Bore Jrs. and just needs minor chip damage for stronger ones. His Wave Immunity is also helpful.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]]: Cat Mask Doron can kill the strongest Bore Jrs., and can reliably hit the frontline, but this is reliant on his Surge Attack connecting. Otherwise, treat him as chip damage.
*Any [[:Category:Cats with Conjure ability|unit with Conjure]], preferably one without too much range, can help provide a burst of damage with their Conjure ability, helping take down Bore Jr.

Bore Jr.'s Wave Attacks make [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] an attractive option. The standard [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] may not be the best here, as its somewhat sluggish speed makes it unresponsive, and it gets shredded once in melee range. [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Ironcat]] is usually a better choice, as he has fast speed, is Resistant to Traitless and can Weaken Bore Jr. While his many knockbacks make him a temporary solution, he usually gets the job done. If you have any ranged Wave Shields, they are much appreciated.

The [[Slow Beam]] is recommended for Bore Jr. stages. Its field-wide coverage and longer debuff duration compared to [[Thunderbolt]] helps reliably shut Bore Jr. down and gives you ample time to formulate a response.

